"""Original forms, lists, task collaboration and visualization cases."""
ITEMS=[]
def group(o,rows):
 for k,(s,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((s,[o[k]]+[v for j,v in enumerate(o) if j!=k],e))
group(['Change the list columns','Configure the form view','Apply a form template','Add the related list'],[
('Agents want to see the assignment group beside the number in a multi-record list without opening each record. Which presentation change fits?', 'Add the relevant list column. This changes the overview, not the detailed form or stored values.'),
('An approved shared form arrangement needs a new section grouping several existing fields. Which configuration task fits?', 'Configure the form view to arrange its fields and sections. A list column change does not arrange the individual-record form.'),
('A technician repeatedly creates a supported type of record with the same approved starting values and wants to populate those values consistently. Which feature fits?', 'A form template populates configured values; it is not a mechanism for moving configuration between instances.'),
('A record form should show a collection of associated child records beneath its main fields. Which presentation element fits?', 'A related list exposes the associated records rather than representing them as ordinary fields on the parent.')])
group(['Join the conditions with AND','Join the alternatives with OR','Use an is-empty condition','Follow the reference with dot-walking'],[
('A list must show only records that are both active and assigned to the Network group. Which condition design implements both requirements?', 'AND requires both conditions to hold. OR would also admit records satisfying only one.'),
('A review should include records assigned to either the Database group or the Network group. Which condition design expresses those alternatives?', 'OR accepts either alternative. Requiring one single-valued group field to equal both groups would not express the request.'),
('A coordinator needs records with no assigned individual, regardless of which group owns them. Which condition targets the missing value?', 'An is-empty condition tests the unpopulated Assigned to field directly.'),
('An incident filter must use the department of its referenced caller rather than a department field stored directly on the incident. Which field-selection technique fits?', 'Dot-walking follows a reference to a field on the related record, such as the caller’s department.')])
group(['2 records','3 records','4 records','5 records'],[
('A list contains six records. Three are active; of those three, two belong to Support. The remaining three are inactive. How many match Active is true AND Group is Support?', 'Only the two active Support records satisfy both conditions.'),
('A five-record review shows these pairs of values for Priority and Assigned to: (High, Lee), (Low, empty), (High, empty), (Low, Kim), (Low, Pat). How many match Priority is High OR Assigned to is empty?', 'The first, second and third records match. The third satisfies both alternatives but is counted only once.'),
('Seven records are in a list: three Closed, two Open and two Pending. A filter excludes Closed records and has no other condition. How many records remain?', 'The two Open and two Pending records remain, totaling four.'),
('Eight requests reference callers. Five callers belong to the Sales department and three to Finance. All requests are readable, and each request references one caller. How many match Caller.Department is Sales?', 'Dot-walking evaluates the department on each referenced caller. Five requests match Sales.')])
group(['Use a freeform task board','Use a guided task board','Use a flexible task board','Use a dashboard'],[
('A team wants a board mixing personal tasks and different kinds of task records, with manually managed lanes. Which experience fits?', 'A freeform board supports personal tasks and varied task cards with user-managed lanes.'),
('A manager wants a board whose lanes correspond to values of a field on the underlying tasks, such as their state. Which board type fits?', 'Guided board lanes correspond to field values rather than freely named arbitrary lanes.'),
('A team wants cards drawn from one table filter but wants custom lanes that do not correspond to field values. Which board type fits?', 'A flexible board combines a table-based filter with custom lanes.'),
('A service owner wants several visualizations of workload and performance together, rather than a card-moving task board. Which experience fits?', 'A dashboard brings visualizations together for monitoring and analysis rather than managing individual cards as lanes.')])
group(['Review When to send','Review Who will receive','Review What it will contain','Preview the notification'],[
('An email notification is generated on every update, but the requirement is to send only when the relevant condition is met. Which configuration area should be reviewed?', 'When to send defines the trigger and conditions. Changing the subject or recipient list does not correct an overly broad trigger.'),
('A notification fires at the right time and has the right text, but its recipient list points to the wrong record field. Which configuration area needs correction?', 'Who will receive determines the recipients, including users or groups referenced by record fields.'),
('A notification reaches the correct people at the correct time, but its message omits required context. Which configuration area should be edited?', 'What it will contain defines the message contents, distinct from trigger and recipient selection.'),
('Before enabling outbound delivery, an administrator wants to inspect the rendered message and see which users would receive it. Which supported validation action fits?', 'Preview Notification lets the administrator examine content and recipient outcomes without relying on a live send.')])
group(['A bar visualization','A time-series visualization','A pie or donut visualization','A pivot table visualization'],[
('A manager needs to compare current ticket counts across several assignment groups, with a separate labeled value for each group. Which visualization is well suited?', 'Bars compare values across categories such as assignment groups.'),
('A service owner needs to see how the backlog changes from week to week over several months. Which visualization is designed for that temporal pattern?', 'A time-series visualization presents change over time rather than just a current category breakdown.'),
('A small set of non-overlapping request categories accounts for the whole workload, and the goal is to show each category’s share of that total. Which visualization fits the part-to-whole goal?', 'Pie or donut segments represent parts of a whole when categories and presentation remain suitable.'),
('An analyst wants counts at each combination of assignment group and priority, with row and column totals. Which visualization fits?', 'A pivot table summarizes combinations of dimensions and can display subtotals.')])
group(['Make the field mandatory','Make the field read-only','Hide the field in that UI','Filter the reference choices'],[
('When a form meets a specified condition, a justification must be entered before the intended UI submission can proceed. Which form action addresses this?', 'Making the field mandatory expresses the input requirement in that UI. Separate server-side enforcement may be needed for other write paths.'),
('Users should see a calculated field on the form but should not edit it through that form. Which presentation action fits?', 'Read-only preserves visibility while preventing editing through the affected UI. It is not by itself a complete data authorization control.'),
('A field is irrelevant to one form condition and should not be displayed in that condition. No access restriction is being implemented by this change. Which action fits?', 'Conditional visibility hides the field in the UI. Data security must be implemented separately if access must be denied.'),
('A reference picker should offer only active departments, while preserving the field and allowing a selection. Which configuration fits?', 'A reference qualifier narrows the choices offered by the reference field; it does not itself replace access control.')])
group(['Check the visualization’s filter','Check the aggregation method','Check the grouping field','Check the underlying data access'],[
('A chart excludes resolved records even though its audience expected all records. Its query contains an Active-only condition. Which configuration explains the mismatch?', 'The filter determines which records enter the visualization before aggregation.'),
('A manager expects the number of requests, but the chart adds their monetary values. Which setting should be corrected?', 'The aggregation method determines whether the chart counts records or summarizes a numeric field.'),
('A chart has correct totals but splits them by location instead of assignment group. Which setting explains the wrong breakdown?', 'The grouping field defines the categories used to break down the data.'),
('An administrator sees a complete chart while an ordinary viewer lacks permission to read some underlying records. Which issue must be evaluated before assuming the chart is broken?', 'Evaluate the viewer’s applicable data access. Presentation sharing does not automatically grant all underlying record permissions.')])
group(['Total value','Minimum value','Maximum value','Average value'],[
('A numeric list column contains approved costs of 20, 30 and 40. The manager needs the combined cost, 90. Which list calculation fits?', 'Total adds the values: 20 + 30 + 40 = 90.'),
('A response-time column contains 4, 7 and 9 minutes. An analyst wants the fastest observed response, 4. Which calculation fits?', 'Minimum selects the smallest observed value.'),
('A duration column contains 12, 18 and 15 minutes. An analyst wants the longest observed duration, 18. Which calculation fits?', 'Maximum selects the largest observed value.'),
('A numeric effort column contains 2, 4 and 9 hours. The analyst wants the arithmetic mean, 5 hours. Which calculation fits?', 'Average divides the sum, 15, by the three records, yielding 5.')])
# Four original choose-two cases; options are independently plausible list operations.
ops=['Filter the record population','Sort the displayed records','Group by a categorical field','Calculate a numeric aggregate']
for s,keys,e in [
('An analyst needs only active requests, displayed from newest to oldest. No category breakdown or numeric summary is requested. Choose two list operations that directly satisfy these requirements.',[0,1],'Filter to active requests and sort by the relevant creation date. Grouping or aggregation is not needed for the stated result.'),
('A coordinator needs every record organized into assignment-group sections, with each section ordered by its due date. Choose two list operations.',[1,2],'Grouping creates the assignment-group sections, and sorting orders the records. No filter or numeric calculation is required.'),
('A finance review needs all records split by cost center and a sum of numeric cost within each group. Choose two list operations.',[2,3],'Group by cost center and calculate the numeric total. Sorting does not calculate a total.'),
('A reviewer needs the total numeric effort for only the records matching an approved date range, with no grouped sections. Choose two list operations.',[3,0],'Filter to the required date range and calculate the numeric total over that population.')]:ITEMS.append((s,ops,e,keys))
assert len(ITEMS)==40
